    {
      "number": "909",
      "source_number": "909",
      "figure_refs": [],
      "source_excerpt": "909. 设$N$是自然数的集合，而$Q$是有理数的集合。а) 利用“欧拉圆”表示集合$N$和$Q$之间的包含关系。б) 在作出的图上，用细线条表示集合$Q$内集合$N$的余集(或补集)。举出这个集合里的几个元素。в) 下面的命题是真命题吗？任何有理数都是自然数。",
      "convention_caveat": "This source excerpt does not decide whether N includes zero. Preserve both N={1,2,...} and N0={0,1,2,...}; do not import 913's explicit positive-integer convention into 909.",
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "909-a",
          "coverage": ["Euler inclusion diagram"],
          "answer": "N < Q under either convention for zero.",
          "reason": "Every natural number n is rational because n=n/1; 1/2 is rational but is not natural.",
          "diagram_semantics": "One closed region labelled N entirely and strictly inside a larger closed region labelled Q. Leave a nonempty Q-only region; the sets are neither disjoint nor merely overlapping. The outside of Q is irrelevant to this question."
        },
        {
          "id": "909-b",
          "coverage": ["shade Q-relative complement", "several elements"],
          "answer": "Shade Q \\ N.",
          "shaded_region": "All of the part inside Q and outside N, with N left unshaded. Do not shade the exterior of Q.",
          "examples": ["-1", "1/2", "3/2", "-5/3"],
          "reason": "These are rational numbers and none is natural under either zero convention.",
          "zero_boundary": "If 0 belongs to N0, then 0 is inside N and outside the shaded complement. If N starts at 1, then 0 belongs to the shaded Q \\ N. The set identity is valid in both cases."
        },
        {
          "id": "909-c",
          "coverage": ["proposition direction", "truth value", "reason or counterexample"],
          "proposition": "Every rational number is a natural number.",
          "direction": "Q <= N",
          "truth": false,
          "counterexample": "1/2 belongs to Q but not to N under either convention.",
          "true_reverse": "Every natural number is rational: N <= Q."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "910",
      "source_number": "910",
      "figure_refs": [],
      "source_excerpt": "910. 设$K$是偶数的集合，而$L$是能被$4$整除的数的集合。作“欧拉圆”表示集合$K$和$L$的关系。在作出的图上用细线条表示不能被$4$整除的偶数的集合。下面的命题是真命题吗？а) 要使一个数是偶数，只要使它能被$4$整除就够了。б) 要使一个数是偶数，必须使它能被$4$整除。в) 要使一个数能被$4$整除，只要使它是偶数就够了。г) 要使一个数能被$4$整除，必须使它是偶数。",
      "domain": "Use ordinary integer divisibility: K={2k:k in Z}, L={4k:k in Z}. If the intended ambient domain is restricted to positive integers, intersect both sets with it; the nesting, propositions, and positive witnesses remain unchanged.",
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "910-header",
          "coverage": ["Euler relation diagram", "shade even numbers not divisible by 4"],
          "answer": "L < K; shade K \\ L.",
          "reason": "4k=2(2k), so every multiple of 4 is even. The number 2 is even and not divisible by 4, so inclusion is proper.",
          "diagram_semantics": "A closed region labelled L strictly inside a larger closed region labelled K. Hatch all of K outside L; leave L and the exterior of K unshaded.",
          "shaded_region": "{4k+2:k in Z}, equivalently n congruent to 2 modulo 4.",
          "illustrative_witnesses_not_extra_tasks": ["2", "6", "10"]
        },
        {
          "id": "910-a",
          "coverage": ["sufficiency direction", "truth value", "reason"],
          "proposition": "Divisibility by 4 is sufficient for being even.",
          "direction": "n in L => n in K",
          "truth": true,
          "reason": "If n=4k, then n=2(2k), an even integer."
        },
        {
          "id": "910-b",
          "coverage": ["necessity direction", "truth value", "counterexample"],
          "proposition": "Divisibility by 4 is necessary for being even.",
          "direction": "n in K => n in L",
          "truth": false,
          "counterexample": "2 is even but is not divisible by 4."
        },
        {
          "id": "910-c",
          "coverage": ["sufficiency direction", "truth value", "counterexample"],
          "proposition": "Being even is sufficient for divisibility by 4.",
          "direction": "n in K => n in L",
          "truth": false,
          "counterexample": "2 is even but is not divisible by 4."
        },
        {
          "id": "910-d",
          "coverage": ["necessity direction", "truth value", "reason"],
          "proposition": "Being even is necessary for divisibility by 4.",
          "direction": "n in L => n in K",
          "truth": true,
          "reason": "A multiple of 4 is twice an integer and therefore even."
        }
      ]
    },
